#!/usr/bin/env node
// land — merge the ready PRs of a state file one by one, close their tickets in one documents PR, and say
// in one line per PR what happened. One command the orchestrator runs in the background instead of many
// model calls per merge (skill epic-wave, section 4).
//
//   land <state.json> [--watch]
//
// The merge condition, on the PR's head commit (profile workflow.ci "pr": CI runs on every PR):
//   - no run of the CI workflow (ci_workflow) on the head is queued or in progress — a newer run is coming,
//     even when an older check of ci_check exists;
//   - the latest check run named ci_check is completed with conclusion success;
//   - when the head is not the one the orchestrator verified (prs[].head), the PR's diff from its fork point,
//     outside the tickets root and without `index` lines, is byte-identical on both heads (a rebase that
//     changed nothing in the PR); otherwise the PR waits for the orchestrator to verify the new head: its
//     review and its list of checks were made for the old one;
//   - the commit status `review` is success. A head with no `review` status at all gets it carried from the
//     verified head when that one has `review` success (the diff is the same, see above); the new status
//     says "carried from <old sha>". A `review` that is failure, error or pending on the head is never
//     overwritten;
//   - every commit status of prs[].checks (`check/<name>`; the orchestrator lists the Checks of the Pipeline
//     the project's rules require for this PR) is success on the head — a `skipped` mark is a success status
//     too. These marks are never carried;
//   - the main branch is not red (a PR with main_fix true, the fix of a red main branch or the revert of its culprit,
//     skips this): the push runs of ci_workflow on the branch check the merged PRs together, so the latest one with a
//     verdict must not be red. A run still queued or in progress is passed over (no merge waits the length of a push
//     run); so is a cancelled one, and so is the run of a commit that changed documents only (by docs_only, see
//     below): it may check far less than a run of code. A run's verdict is that of its latest attempt: a red run whose failed jobs were
//     rerun once and passed is green — a flaky test, not the PR's fault. land reruns nothing and reverts nothing.
//     While it is red a PR with code waits with the reason `<branch> red since <sha> (#<PR>, <time>), run <URL> —
//     code PRs wait; fix forward until <time + 1 h>, then revert #<PR>`: the culprit is the PR whose merge commit has
//     the first red push run after the last green one (`gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits/<sha>/pulls`), <time>
//     when that run finished; with no green run among the newest 50, the culprit is older and the reason says to find
//     it by hand. A PR with documents only still merges: docs_only, the project's rule, gets the PR's changed paths
//     and exits 0. The newest run being rerun holds code PRs until its verdict. gh unable to read the
//     runs — the PR waits (unverified), never merges;
//   - then, under the main-branch lock (mkdir of main_lock, by default <git common dir>/main.lock — the lock
//     the skills share): `mergeable` UNKNOWN is asked again up to MERGEABLE_RETRIES times, RETRY_S apart;
//     CONFLICTING or DIRTY — the PR waits with "conflict: rebase" (land rebases nothing); the head must still
//     be the checked one; the CI check, the marks and the main branch are read again (the lock may have been waited for a long
//     time); then `gh pr merge <N> --squash --match-head-commit <head>`.
//     A base that moved is no reason to wait: a PR is not rebased only to get a fresh base, the CI run on the
//     push to the main branch checks the merged PRs together. With branch protection `strict` false GitHub
//     does not report BEHIND for such a PR; with `strict` true it reports BEHIND and
//     refuses the merge itself — that refusal is the wait, with the reason "BEHIND: the base branch requires
//     an up-to-date branch, rebase".
// A PR that waits does not hold back the next one: each PR is merged on its own head's condition, in the
// order of the state file. No local gate runs here, and workflow.ci "batch" is refused: with it a PR head has no CI run to merge on
// (wave-gate is that path).
//
// After the merges: one documents PR per run of land. In a worktree of its own (<state>.docs, a branch
// land-docs/<time> from <remote>/<branch>), for every merged PR not yet in a documents PR: one
// `ticket evidence <epic> <NN> <item> <kind> <verdict> --ref <ref> [--platform P] --copy C --sha S --root
// <tree>/<tickets root>` per entry of prs[].evidence (the Evidence lines of the review verdict and the green CI
// check, which the orchestrator knows before the merge: written into the branch after CI they would make a new
// head and one more CI run), then `ticket done <epic> <NN> --pr <N> --root <tree>/<tickets root>`. Then
// docs_check, `git add -A`, the privacy check `evidence-check --changed --root <tree>/<tickets root> --base
// refs/remotes/<remote>/<branch>` (exit 1 — the findings, masked, go to the log; the documents wait red, nothing
// is committed or pushed), a commit, a push, `gh pr create`. That PR merges on ci_check alone (documents get no
// agent review) under the same lock. A documents PR closed without a merge does not cover its tickets: the same
// entry gets a new branch and a new PR. With tickets_root null there is no documents PR: prs[].evidence is not
// written, and land prints `evidence of #N is the orchestrator's (tickets outside the repository)`.
//
// The state file is the input and the record; every finished step is written to it at once, so a run
// broken off (the session ended, a kill) goes on from there when it is run again on the same file: a PR
// recorded as merged, or one GitHub already shows as merged, is never merged again. The orchestrator writes:
//   repo          absolute path of a checkout of the main branch (git and gh run here)
//   branch        the main branch; remote — optional, "origin"
//   ci            profile workflow.ci: "pr" (anything else — exit 1)
//   ci_check      the name of the check run that is the merge condition
//   ci_workflow   the workflow (file name) of the CI runs on a PR head
//   docs_check    null, or a shell command run in the documents worktree before its commit (profile
//                 docs.handoff.check)
//   docs_only     optional, null or a shell command run in the checkout: the paths a PR changes from its fork point,
//                 one per line on stdin; exit 0 — documents only (the PR merges while the main branch is red), 1 —
//                 code; any other exit code counts as code. No command: documents only means every path inside the
//                 tickets root. The same rule tells a push run of a documents-only commit, which gives no verdict
//   tickets_root  optional, ".scratch": the tickets root, relative to the repository root (profile
//                 tickets.root; an absolute one the orchestrator makes relative); null — the tickets are not
//                 in the repository (Silent mode, a root outside it), no documents PR: `ticket done` is the
//                 orchestrator's
//   main_lock     optional absolute path of the main-branch lock
//   prs           [{number, epic, ticket, head, checks, evidence, main_fix}] in merge order; epic and ticket — the PR's ticket
//                 (without them no `ticket done`); head — optional, the head SHA the review verified; checks —
//                 the Check marks the PR needs, ["windows"] or ["check/windows"] alike, [] for none; evidence —
//                 optional, [{item, kind, verdict, ref, platform?, copy?, sha?}]: the Evidence lines `ticket
//                 evidence` writes before `ticket done` (item — the checkbox item of the "done" section, from 1). The
//                 defaults: sha — prs[].head (an entry without a sha needs it), platform — "-" for review and commit,
//                 "ci" for ci-check, otherwise the one `ticket` takes, copy — "-"; main_fix — optional, true for the
//                 fix of a red main branch or the revert of its culprit: it merges while the branch is red
// land adds: prs[].result {status: merged|waits, sha | reason, kind, at}, docs [{branch, prs, pr, closed,
// result}], runs [{started, ended, land}].
//
// Output: one line per PR, `#N merged <sha>` or `#N waits: <reason>`, the documents PR the same way; while the
// main branch is red, the line `<branch> red since <sha> (#<PR>, <time>) — code PRs wait; fix forward until
// <time + 1 h>, then revert #<PR>`; then `LAND=green` (every PR and the documents PR merged), `LAND=red` (a PR waits
// on a red verdict: a red or cancelled check, a review or Check mark failure, a red docs_check) or `LAND=unverified`
// (something waits for CI, a person, a rebase or the fix of a red main branch — not the PR's own red). Exit 0 green, 2 red, 3 unverified, 1 error in the input. The full log goes
// to <state>.log.
//
// --watch: passes every POLL_S seconds while a PR or the documents PR waits for CI (a run in progress, a
// check not finished, mergeable UNKNOWN), at most WATCH_S seconds in all. Without it — one pass.
//
// Environment (tests set them; the defaults are the project's): LAND_GH, LAND_TICKET, LAND_EVIDENCE_CHECK,
// LAND_SLEEP — an executable used instead of `gh`, of bin/ticket and bin/evidence-check next to this script and
// of the wait between tries (it gets the seconds); a `.mjs` file runs with this node. LAND_POLL_S (300),
// LAND_WATCH_S (6600), LAND_RETRY_S (10), LAND_LOCK_POLL_S (30), LAND_LOCK_STALE_S (5400: the 90 minutes after
// which the skills call the lock stuck).
// shortcut: two runs of land on one state file are not kept apart, redo with a pid file like wave-gate's once a second
// run is ever started (each merge is still guarded by the lock and --match-head-commit; the file is not).
"use strict"
const fs = require("fs")
const path = require("path")
const { spawnSync } = require("child_process")
// The git to start, with the variable of an eval run (EVAL_GIT).
const { git: GIT } = require("../hooks/eval-env.cjs")
// The Evidence kinds that name no machine: their platform is "-".
const { NO_MACHINE } = require("../lib/evidence.cjs")

const SHA = /^[0-9a-f]{40}$/
const MERGEABLE_RETRIES = 6
const seconds = (name, dflt) => {
    const v = Number(process.env[name])
    return Number.isFinite(v) && v > 0 ? v : dflt
}
const T = {
    poll: seconds("LAND_POLL_S", 300),
    watch: seconds("LAND_WATCH_S", 6600),
    retry: seconds("LAND_RETRY_S", 10),
    lockPoll: seconds("LAND_LOCK_POLL_S", 30),
    lockStale: seconds("LAND_LOCK_STALE_S", 5400),
}
const SIGNALS = { SIGHUP: 1, SIGINT: 2, SIGTERM: 15, ...(process.platform === "win32" ? { SIGBREAK: 21 } : {}) }

class Fail extends Error {}
const fail = (msg) => {
    throw new Fail(msg)
}
// Why a PR is not merged. kind: "red" — a red verdict; "ci" — CI has not answered yet, a later pass may merge it;
// "waits" — someone has to act (a review, a rebase, another machine's verdict) or gh could not be read.
class Wait extends Error {
    constructor(reason, kind = "waits") {
        super(reason)
        this.kind = kind
    }
}
const now = () => new Date().toISOString().replace(/\.\d+Z$/, "Z")
const short = (sha) => (sha || "").slice(0, 8)
const firstLine = (s) => (s || "").trim().split("\n")[0]

let logFile = null
const log = (msg) => {
    if (logFile) fs.appendFileSync(logFile, `${now()} ${msg}\n`)
}
// The main-branch lock this process holds, released on every way out (a signal included; a SIGKILL leaves it,
// and LAND_LOCK_STALE_S later it counts as stuck).
let heldLock = null
function unlock() {
    if (!heldLock) return
    try {
        fs.rmdirSync(heldLock)
        log(`released the main-branch lock ${heldLock}`)
    } catch {}
    heldLock = null
}

// [file, args] of a program a test may stand in for: `usual` without an override, a `.mjs` override with this node.
function program(override, usual) {
    if (!override) return usual
    if (override.endsWith(".mjs")) return [process.execPath, [override]]
    return [override, []]
}
function run([file, pre], args, cwd) {
    const r = spawnSync(file, [...pre, ...args], { cwd, encoding: "utf8", windowsHide: true, maxBuffer: 64 << 20 })
    return { code: r.error ? 127 : (r.status ?? 128 + (SIGNALS[r.signal] || 0)), out: r.stdout || "", err: r.error ? r.error.message : r.stderr || "" }
}
const sh = (command, cwd, input) => {
    const r = spawnSync(command, { cwd, input, encoding: "utf8", windowsHide: true, shell: true, maxBuffer: 64 << 20 })
    return { code: r.error ? 127 : (r.status ?? 128 + (SIGNALS[r.signal] || 0)), out: r.stdout || "", err: r.stderr || "" }
}
async function sleep(s) {
    if (process.env.LAND_SLEEP) {
        run(program(process.env.LAND_SLEEP, null), [String(s)])
        return
    }
    await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, s * 1000))
}

// --- the state file ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
function load(file) {
    let st
    try {
        st = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, "utf8"))
    } catch (e) {
        fail(`${file}: ${e.message}`)
    }
    if (!st || typeof st !== "object" || Array.isArray(st)) fail(`${file} is not a JSON object`)
    const text = (key) => typeof st[key] === "string" && st[key].trim() !== ""
    if (!text("repo") || !path.isAbsolute(st.repo) || !fs.existsSync(st.repo)) fail(`${file}: "repo" must be the absolute path of a checkout`)
    if (!text("branch")) fail(`${file}: "branch" must name the main branch`)
    if (st.remote !== undefined && !text("remote")) fail(`${file}: "remote" must be a remote name`)
    if (st.ci !== "pr")
        fail(`${file}: "ci" is ${JSON.stringify(st.ci)}: land merges on the CI check of a PR head, which only workflow.ci "pr" has (with "batch" — wave-gate)`)
    if (!text("ci_check")) fail(`${file}: "ci_check" must name the check run that is the merge condition`)
    if (!text("ci_workflow")) fail(`${file}: "ci_workflow" must name the workflow of the CI runs on a PR head`)
    if ("scope" in st) fail(`${file}: "scope" is not read any more: list the Check marks each PR needs in its "checks"`)
    if (!("docs_check" in st)) fail(`${file}: "docs_check" must be present (null for none): a missing one would silently run without it`)
    if (st.docs_check !== null && !text("docs_check")) fail(`${file}: "docs_check" must be null or a command`)
    if (
        st.tickets_root !== undefined &&
        st.tickets_root !== null &&
        !(
            text("tickets_root") &&
            !path.isAbsolute(st.tickets_root) &&
            !path.normalize(st.tickets_root).startsWith("..") &&
            // the repository itself would exclude the whole diff from the comparison of two heads
            ![".", ""].includes(path.normalize(st.tickets_root).replace(/[\\/]+$/, ""))
        )
    )
        fail(`${file}: "tickets_root" must be a folder inside the repository, relative to its root, or null`)
    if (st.main_lock !== undefined && st.main_lock !== null && (typeof st.main_lock !== "string" || !path.isAbsolute(st.main_lock)))
        fail(`${file}: "main_lock" must be an absolute path`)
    if (st.docs_only !== undefined && st.docs_only !== null && !text("docs_only")) fail(`${file}: "docs_only" must be null or a command`)
    if (!Array.isArray(st.prs) || !st.prs.length) fail(`${file}: "prs" must be a list of PRs`)
    const seen = new Set()
    for (const pr of st.prs) {
        if (!pr || !Number.isInteger(pr.number) || pr.number <= 0) fail(`${file}: every PR needs a positive integer "number"`)
        if (seen.has(pr.number)) fail(`${file}: PR #${pr.number} is listed twice`)
        seen.add(pr.number)
        if (pr.head !== undefined && pr.head !== null && !SHA.test(pr.head)) fail(`${file}: PR #${pr.number}: "head" must be a full SHA`)
        if (pr.main_fix !== undefined && pr.main_fix !== null && typeof pr.main_fix !== "boolean") fail(`${file}: PR #${pr.number}: "main_fix" must be true or false`)
        for (const key of ["epic", "ticket"])
            if (pr[key] !== undefined && pr[key] !== null && (typeof pr[key] !== "string" || !pr[key])) fail(`${file}: PR #${pr.number}: "${key}" must be a string`)
        // a missing list would merge without the Checks the project requires
        if (!Array.isArray(pr.checks) || !pr.checks.every((c) => typeof c === "string" && /^(check\/)?[^\s/]+$/.test(c)))
            fail(`${file}: PR #${pr.number}: "checks" must be a list of Check names ([] for none)`)
        if (pr.evidence !== undefined && pr.evidence !== null) {
            const word = (e, key) => typeof e[key] === "string" && e[key] !== ""
            const maybe = (e, key) => e[key] === undefined || e[key] === null || word(e, key)
            const entry = (e) =>
                e && typeof e === "object" && Number.isInteger(e.item) && e.item > 0 && ["kind", "verdict", "ref"].every((k) => word(e, k)) && ["platform", "copy", "sha"].every((k) => maybe(e, k))
            if (!Array.isArray(pr.evidence) || !pr.evidence.every(entry))
                fail(`${file}: PR #${pr.number}: "evidence" must be a list of {item, kind, verdict, ref, platform?, copy?, sha?} (item from 1)`)
            // with no documents PR (tickets_root null) the entries are the orchestrator's and need nothing more here
            if (st.tickets_root !== null && pr.evidence.length) {
                if (!pr.epic || !pr.ticket) fail(`${file}: PR #${pr.number}: "evidence" needs the PR's "epic" and "ticket"`)
                if (!pr.head && !pr.evidence.every((e) => e.sha)) fail(`${file}: PR #${pr.number}: an "evidence" entry without a "sha" needs the PR's "head"`)
            }
        }
    }
    st.docs = Array.isArray(st.docs) ? st.docs : []
    st.runs = Array.isArray(st.runs) ? st.runs : []
    return st
}
function save(file, st) {
    const tmp = `${file}.tmp-${process.pid}`
    fs.writeFileSync(tmp, JSON.stringify(st, null, 2) + "\n")
    fs.renameSync(tmp, file)
}

// --- git and gh ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
function git(args, cwd) {
    const r = run([GIT, []], args, cwd)
    if (r.code !== 0) throw new Wait(`git ${args.join(" ")} (exit ${r.code}): ${firstLine(r.err)}`)
    return r.out.trim()
}
function gh(st, args) {
    const r = run(program(process.env.LAND_GH, ["gh", []]), args, st.repo)
    log(`gh ${args.join(" ")} — exit ${r.code}`)
    return r
}
function ghJson(st, args, what) {
    const r = gh(st, args)
    if (r.code !== 0) throw new Wait(`${what}: gh exit ${r.code}: ${firstLine(r.err)}`)
    try {
        return JSON.parse(r.out)
    } catch {
        throw new Wait(`${what}: gh printed no JSON`)
    }
}
const PR_FIELDS = "number,state,headRefOid,mergeable,mergeStateStatus,mergeCommit"
const prView = (st, n) => ghJson(st, ["pr", "view", String(n), "--json", PR_FIELDS], `gh pr view ${n}`)
// The commit statuses of a commit, the latest per context: {context: {state, description}}.
function statuses(st, sha) {
    const s = ghJson(st, ["api", `repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits/${sha}/status?per_page=100`], `the statuses of ${short(sha)}`)
    const out = {}
    for (const x of Array.isArray(s.statuses) ? s.statuses : []) if (x && x.context && !out[x.context]) out[x.context] = x
    return out
}

// --- the merge condition ------------------------------------------------------------------------
function ciGreen(st, head) {
    const runs = ghJson(st, ["run", "list", "--workflow", st.ci_workflow, "--commit", head, "--limit", "20", "--json", "databaseId,status,conclusion"], `the ${st.ci_workflow} runs`)
    const open = (Array.isArray(runs) ? runs : []).filter((r) => r.status !== "completed")
    if (open.length) throw new Wait(`${st.ci_workflow} run ${open[0].databaseId} is ${open[0].status} on ${short(head)}`, "ci")
    const cr = ghJson(st, ["api", `repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits/${head}/check-runs?per_page=100`], `the check runs of ${short(head)}`)
    const mine = (Array.isArray(cr.check_runs) ? cr.check_runs : [])
        .filter((c) => c.name === st.ci_check)
        .sort((a, b) => String(a.started_at || "").localeCompare(String(b.started_at || "")) || (a.id || 0) - (b.id || 0))
    const last = mine[mine.length - 1]
    if (!last) throw new Wait(`no ${st.ci_check} check on ${short(head)}`, "ci")
    if (last.status !== "completed") throw new Wait(`${st.ci_check} is ${last.status} on ${short(head)}`, "ci")
    if (last.conclusion !== "success") throw new Wait(`${st.ci_check} ${last.conclusion} on ${short(head)}`, "red")
}
// The PR's diff from its fork point off the main branch, outside the tickets root, without the `index` lines
// (blob ids change with a rebase even when the change does not).
function prDiff(st, sha) {
    const remote = st.remote || "origin"
    const base = git(["merge-base", sha, `refs/remotes/${remote}/${st.branch}`], st.repo)
    const d = git(["diff", "--binary", base, sha, "--", ".", `:(exclude)${st.tickets_root || ".scratch"}`], st.repo)
    return d
        .split("\n")
        .filter((l) => !l.startsWith("index "))
        .join("\n")
}
function haveCommit(st, sha, n) {
    if (run([GIT, []], ["cat-file", "-e", `${sha}^{commit}`], st.repo).code === 0) return true
    run([GIT, []], ["fetch", "-q", st.remote || "origin", sha], st.repo)
    if (n) run([GIT, []], ["fetch", "-q", st.remote || "origin", `refs/pull/${n}/head`], st.repo)
    return run([GIT, []], ["cat-file", "-e", `${sha}^{commit}`], st.repo).code === 0
}
// The review and the list of checks are the orchestrator's for the head it verified (prs[].head). Another head
// passes only when the PR's change is the same on it: a rebase with nothing new.
function sameChange(st, pr, head) {
    const old = pr.head
    if (!old || old === head) return
    if (!haveCommit(st, old, pr.number) || !haveCommit(st, head, pr.number)) throw new Wait(`the head moved from ${short(old)} to ${short(head)}, and git has not got both to compare`)
    if (prDiff(st, old) !== prDiff(st, head))
        throw new Wait(`the head moved from ${short(old)} to ${short(head)} and the PR's change differs: verify the new head and put it in the state file`)
}
const red = (state) => (state === "failure" || state === "error" ? "red" : "waits")
// The `review` mark on the head. carry — a head with no `review` status at all may get the verified head's
// success (sameChange has passed); a failure or pending review on the head is a reviewer's and stays.
function reviewed(st, pr, head, marks, carry) {
    const mark = marks.review
    if (mark && mark.state === "success") return
    const old = pr.head
    if (!mark && carry && old && old !== head) {
        const was = statuses(st, old).review
        if (was && was.state === "success") {
            const description = `carried from ${short(old)}: the PR diff outside ${st.tickets_root || ".scratch"} is unchanged`
            const r = gh(st, ["api", "-X", "POST", `repos/{owner}/{repo}/statuses/${head}`, "-f", "state=success", "-f", "context=review", "-f", `description=${description}`])
            if (r.code !== 0) throw new Wait(`review could not be carried to ${short(head)}: gh exit ${r.code}: ${firstLine(r.err)}`)
            log(`#${pr.number}: review ${description}, now on ${head}`)
            return
        }
    }
    const state = mark ? mark.state : "missing"
    throw new Wait(`review is ${state} on ${short(head)}`, red(state))
}
// The Check marks the PR needs (prs[].checks), each success on the head (`skipped` is posted as success).
function checked(pr, head, marks) {
    for (const name of pr.checks) {
        const context = name.startsWith("check/") ? name : `check/${name}`
        const mark = marks[context]
        if (mark && mark.state === "success") continue
        const state = mark ? mark.state : "missing"
        throw new Wait(`${context} is ${state} on ${short(head)}`, red(state))
    }
}
// --- the main branch: its push runs check the merged PRs together --------------------------------------
// The push runs of the CI workflow on the main branch, newest first (a push run per commit: none cancels another).
// The latest one with a verdict decides: success — green; failure, timed_out, startup_failure — red. A run still
// queued or in progress has no verdict yet and is passed over, so no merge waits the length of a push run; a
// cancelled, skipped or neutral one says nothing about the code and is passed over too, and so does the run of a
// commit that changed documents only (pathsAreDocuments): such a run may check far less than a run of code (a project
// may run only its lint for documents), so its green must not clear a red run of code below it. A run's conclusion is that
// of its latest attempt: a red run whose failed jobs were rerun and passed is green (a flaky test, not a broken
// branch). A run newer than every verdict that is being rerun (attempt above 1, not completed) holds code PRs
// until its verdict: only a finished run is rerun, and it is rerun because it was red.
const MAIN_RUNS = 50
const VERDICT = { success: "green", failure: "red", timed_out: "red", startup_failure: "red" }
const plusHour = (t) => {
    const ms = Date.parse(t)
    return Number.isFinite(ms) ? new Date(ms + 3600e3).toISOString().replace(/\.\d+Z$/, "Z") : "an hour after it"
}
const culprits = new Map()
// The PR whose merge commit sha is: "#N", or null for a commit with no PR (a direct push) or one gh cannot tell.
function culpritPr(st, sha) {
    if (culprits.has(sha)) return culprits.get(sha)
    const r = gh(st, ["api", `repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits/${sha}/pulls`])
    let pr = null
    try {
        const list = r.code === 0 ? JSON.parse(r.out) : []
        const mine = (Array.isArray(list) ? list : []).filter((p) => p && Number.isInteger(p.number))
        // only the PR this commit merged: a PR that merely contains the commit is not its merge
        const hit = mine.find((p) => p.merge_commit_sha === sha)
        if (hit) pr = `#${hit.number}`
    } catch {}
    if (r.code !== 0) log(`the PRs of ${short(sha)}: gh exit ${r.code}: ${firstLine(r.err)}`)
    culprits.set(sha, pr)
    return pr
}
// A wait on the main branch's verdict (red, or a rerun of a red run), not on gh: a PR with documents only may still merge.
const mainWait = (reason, kind) => Object.assign(new Wait(reason, kind), { main: true })
// The line for the orchestrator while the main branch is red, from the last reading of its push runs (null — not red).
let mainRed = null
// Whether the commit sha of the main branch changed documents only (pathsAreDocuments over its diff with its first
// parent); a commit git cannot get counts as code, so its run keeps its verdict.
const docCommits = new Map()
function documentsCommit(st, sha) {
    if (docCommits.has(sha)) return docCommits.get(sha)
    let docs = false
    if (st.docs_only || ticketsRoot(st)) {
        try {
            if (haveCommit(st, sha)) {
                const paths = git(["-c", "core.quotePath=false", "diff-tree", "-r", "--root", "--no-commit-id", "--name-only", "--no-renames", "-z", "-m", "--first-parent", sha], st.repo).split("\0").filter(Boolean)
                docs = pathsAreDocuments(st, paths, `the commit ${short(sha)}`)
            }
        } catch (e) {
            if (!(e instanceof Wait)) throw e
            log(`the commit ${short(sha)}: documents only? ${e.message} — counted as code`)
        }
    }
    docCommits.set(sha, docs)
    return docs
}
// The state of the main branch: throws Wait when a PR with code may not merge now. The culprit is the first red push
// run after the last green one. With no green one among the newest MAIN_RUNS, the culprit is older than they are, unless
// they are the whole history of the branch.
function mainGreen(st) {
    const what = `the ${st.ci_workflow} push runs on ${st.branch}`
    const runs = ghJson(st, ["run", "list", "--workflow", st.ci_workflow, "--branch", st.branch, "--event", "push", "--limit", String(MAIN_RUNS), "--json", "databaseId,headSha,status,conclusion,attempt,createdAt,updatedAt,url"], what)
    if (!Array.isArray(runs)) throw new Wait(`${what}: gh printed no list`)
    const newest = [...runs].sort((a, b) => String(b.createdAt || "").localeCompare(String(a.createdAt || "")) || (b.databaseId || 0) - (a.databaseId || 0))
    let first = null
    let running = false
    let green = false
    for (const r of newest) {
        if (r.status !== "completed") {
            if (!first && Number(r.attempt) > 1) {
                mainRed = null
                throw mainWait(`the push run ${r.url || r.databaseId} on ${st.branch} (${short(r.headSha)}) is being rerun (attempt ${r.attempt}): code PRs wait for its verdict`, "ci")
            }
            if (!first) running = true
            continue
        }
        const verdict = VERDICT[r.conclusion]
        if (!verdict) continue
        if (documentsCommit(st, r.headSha)) {
            log(`push run ${r.databaseId} on ${short(r.headSha)} (${r.conclusion}): documents only, no verdict on the code`)
            continue
        }
        if (verdict === "green") {
            green = true
            break
        }
        first = r
    }
    if (!first) {
        mainRed = null
        return
    }
    if (!green && runs.length >= MAIN_RUNS) {
        const since = first.updatedAt || first.createdAt
        mainRed = `${st.branch} red since before ${short(first.headSha)} (no green push run among the newest ${MAIN_RUNS}, the oldest red one ${since}) — code PRs wait; the culprit is older than these runs: find it by hand`
        throw mainWait(`${mainRed.replace(" — ", `, run ${first.url || first.databaseId} — `)}`, running ? "ci" : "waits")
    }
    const pr = culpritPr(st, first.headSha)
    const since = first.updatedAt || first.createdAt
    const head = `${st.branch} red since ${short(first.headSha)} (${pr || "no PR"}, ${since})`
    const tail = `code PRs wait; fix forward until ${plusHour(since)}, then revert ${pr || short(first.headSha)}`
    mainRed = `${head} — ${tail}`
    // a newer run in progress may bring the green verdict: a later pass may merge (--watch keeps asking)
    throw mainWait(`${head}, run ${first.url || first.databaseId} — ${tail}`, running ? "ci" : "waits")
}
// The tickets root inside the repository, or null (tickets_root null: the tickets are elsewhere).
const ticketsRoot = (st) => (st.tickets_root === null ? null : (st.tickets_root || ".scratch").replace(/[\\/]+$/, ""))
// Whether paths are documents only, by the project's rule (docs_only): the paths go to the command on stdin, one per line;
// exit 0 — documents only, 1 — code, any other exit code — code. With no rule: every path inside the tickets root (the
// documents PR of land itself). No path at all: code.
function pathsAreDocuments(st, paths, what) {
    if (!paths.length) return false
    if (!st.docs_only) {
        const root = ticketsRoot(st)
        return !!root && paths.every((x) => x.startsWith(`${root}/`))
    }
    const r = sh(st.docs_only, st.repo, paths.map((x) => `${x}\n`).join(""))
    log(`${what}: ${st.docs_only} — exit ${r.code}${r.code > 1 ? `: ${firstLine(r.err || r.out)}` : ""}`)
    return r.code === 0
}
// Whether the PR at head changes documents only (pathsAreDocuments over its diff from its fork point). A head git cannot
// get: code.
function documentsOnly(st, pr, head) {
    try {
        if (!haveCommit(st, head, pr.number)) return false
        const base = git(["merge-base", head, `refs/remotes/${st.remote || "origin"}/${st.branch}`], st.repo)
        // -z: a path as it is, not quoted (non-ASCII letters, spaces)
        const paths = git(["-c", "core.quotePath=false", "diff", "--name-only", "--no-renames", "-z", base, head], st.repo).split("\0").filter(Boolean)
        return pathsAreDocuments(st, paths, `#${pr.number}`)
    } catch (e) {
        if (!(e instanceof Wait)) throw e
        log(`#${pr.number}: documents only? ${e.message} — counted as code`)
        return false
    }
}
// The main branch's condition of a PR: a fix of the red branch (main_fix) and a PR with documents only merge while it is red.
function mainAllows(st, pr, head) {
    if (pr.main_fix) return
    try {
        mainGreen(st)
    } catch (e) {
        if (!(e instanceof Wait) || !e.main || !documentsOnly(st, pr, head)) throw e
        log(`#${pr.number}: documents only, merged while ${st.branch} is red`)
    }
}
// The whole merge condition of a code PR on head; carry — whether a missing review may be carried.
function ready(st, pr, head, carry) {
    ciGreen(st, head)
    sameChange(st, pr, head)
    const marks = statuses(st, head)
    reviewed(st, pr, head, marks, carry)
    checked(pr, head, marks)
    mainAllows(st, pr, head)
}

// --- the merge, under the main-branch lock -------------------------------------------------------------
async function lock(dir) {
    let told = false
    for (;;) {
        try {
            fs.mkdirSync(dir)
            heldLock = dir
            log(`took the main-branch lock ${dir}`)
            return
        } catch (e) {
            if (e.code !== "EEXIST") throw new Wait(`the main-branch lock ${dir}: ${e.message}`)
        }
        let m
        try {
            m = fs.statSync(dir).mtimeMs
        } catch {
            continue // released between mkdir and stat
        }
        if ((Date.now() - m) / 1000 > T.lockStale) {
            log(`the main-branch lock ${dir} is older than ${T.lockStale} s — stuck, removed`)
            try {
                fs.rmdirSync(dir)
            } catch {}
            continue
        }
        if (!told) log(`waiting for the main-branch lock ${dir}`)
        told = true
        await sleep(T.lockPoll)
    }
}
// Merges PR n at head; returns the merge commit. Throws Wait when it may not merge now. verify — the merge
// condition, read again under the lock: the lock may have been waited for long enough for a mark or a run to change.
async function mergeOne(st, n, head, verify) {
    await lock(st.main_lock || path.join(git(["rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir"], st.repo), "main.lock"))
    try {
        let v
        for (let retry = 0; ; retry++) {
            v = prView(st, n)
            if (v.state === "MERGED") return (v.mergeCommit && v.mergeCommit.oid) || "unknown"
            if (v.state !== "OPEN") throw new Wait(`the PR is ${v.state}`)
            if (v.headRefOid !== head) throw new Wait(`the head moved from ${short(head)} to ${short(v.headRefOid)} during the check`, "ci")
            if (v.mergeable !== "UNKNOWN" || retry >= MERGEABLE_RETRIES) break
            log(`#${n}: mergeable UNKNOWN, asking again in ${T.retry} s (retry ${retry + 1} of ${MERGEABLE_RETRIES})`)
            await sleep(T.retry)
        }
        if (v.mergeable === "UNKNOWN") throw new Wait(`mergeable UNKNOWN after ${MERGEABLE_RETRIES} retries`, "ci")
        if (v.mergeable === "CONFLICTING" || v.mergeStateStatus === "DIRTY")
            throw new Wait(`conflict: rebase — the PR conflicts with its base (mergeable ${v.mergeable}, mergeStateStatus ${v.mergeStateStatus})`)
        // BEHIND without a conflict merges like CLEAN: a fresh base is no merge condition (GitHub refuses it under strict protection)
        const behind = v.mergeStateStatus === "BEHIND"
        if (behind) log(`#${n}: BEHIND without a conflict — merging without a rebase`)
        verify()
        const r = gh(st, ["pr", "merge", String(n), "--squash", "--match-head-commit", head])
        if (r.code !== 0 && behind)
            throw new Wait(`BEHIND: the base branch requires an up-to-date branch, rebase — gh pr merge exit ${r.code}: ${firstLine(r.err)}`)
        if (r.code !== 0) throw new Wait(`gh pr merge failed (exit ${r.code}): ${firstLine(r.err)}`)
        let sha = null
        try {
            const after = prView(st, n)
            sha = after.mergeCommit && after.mergeCommit.oid
        } catch {}
        return sha || "unknown"
    } finally {
        unlock()
    }
}

// --- one pass over the PRs ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
async function landPr(file, st, pr) {
    if (pr.result && pr.result.status === "merged") return
    try {
        const v = prView(st, pr.number)
        let sha
        if (v.state === "MERGED") {
            sha = (v.mergeCommit && v.mergeCommit.oid) || "unknown"
            log(`#${pr.number}: GitHub shows it merged already (${sha}), recorded`)
        } else {
            if (v.state !== "OPEN") throw new Wait(`the PR is ${v.state}`)
            const head = v.headRefOid
            ready(st, pr, head, true)
            sha = await mergeOne(st, pr.number, head, () => ready(st, pr, head, false))
            log(`#${pr.number}: merged at ${head} as ${sha}`)
        }
        pr.result = { status: "merged", sha, at: now() }
    } catch (e) {
        if (!(e instanceof Wait)) throw e
        pr.result = { status: "waits", reason: e.message, kind: e.kind, at: now() }
        log(`#${pr.number} waits: ${e.message}`)
    }
    save(file, st)
}

const docsBranch = (n) => `land-docs/${now().replace(/[-:]/g, "").replace(/Z$/, "")}${n ? "-" + n : ""}`
// The documents PR of this run: every merged PR with a ticket that no documents PR has yet.
function docsEntry(file, st, madeThisRun) {
    if (st.tickets_root === null) return
    const covered = new Set(st.docs.flatMap((d) => d.prs))
    const todo = st.prs.filter((p) => p.result && p.result.status === "merged" && p.epic && p.ticket && !covered.has(p.number)).map((p) => p.number)
    if (!todo.length) return
    // an entry whose PR was never opened takes the new ones; otherwise one new entry per run
    const open = st.docs.find((d) => !d.pr)
    if (open) open.prs.push(...todo)
    else if (!madeThisRun.done) st.docs.push({ branch: docsBranch(), prs: todo, pr: null, result: null })
    else return
    madeThisRun.done = true
    save(file, st)
}
// The arguments of `ticket evidence` for an entry of prs[].evidence (load has checked its shape).
function evidenceArgs(p, e, root) {
    const platform = e.platform || (NO_MACHINE.includes(e.kind) ? "-" : e.kind === "ci-check" ? "ci" : null)
    return ["evidence", p.epic, p.ticket, String(e.item), e.kind, e.verdict, "--ref", e.ref, ...(platform ? ["--platform", platform] : []), "--copy", e.copy || "-", "--sha", e.sha || p.head, "--root", root]
}
function openDocsPr(file, st, d) {
    const remote = st.remote || "origin"
    const tree = `${file}.docs`
    const root = st.tickets_root || ".scratch"
    run([GIT, []], ["worktree", "remove", "--force", tree], st.repo)
    fs.rmSync(tree, { recursive: true, force: true })
    run([GIT, []], ["worktree", "prune"], st.repo)
    git(["fetch", "-q", remote, `+refs/heads/${st.branch}:refs/remotes/${remote}/${st.branch}`], st.repo)
    git(["worktree", "add", "-q", "-B", d.branch, tree, `refs/remotes/${remote}/${st.branch}`], st.repo)
    try {
        const ticket = program(process.env.LAND_TICKET, [process.execPath, [path.join(__dirname, "ticket")]])
        for (const n of d.prs) {
            const p = st.prs.find((x) => x.number === n)
            for (const e of p.evidence || []) {
                const args = evidenceArgs(p, e, path.join(tree, root))
                const r = run(ticket, args, tree)
                log(`ticket ${args.join(" ")} — exit ${r.code}`)
                if (r.code !== 0) throw new Wait(`ticket evidence ${p.epic} ${p.ticket} ${e.item} ${e.kind} failed (exit ${r.code}): ${firstLine(r.err)}`)
            }
            const args = ["done", p.epic, p.ticket, "--pr", String(n), "--root", path.join(tree, root)]
            const r = run(ticket, args, tree)
            log(`ticket ${args.join(" ")} — exit ${r.code}`)
            if (r.code !== 0) throw new Wait(`ticket done ${p.epic} ${p.ticket} failed (exit ${r.code}): ${firstLine(r.err)}`)
        }
        if (st.docs_check) {
            const r = sh(st.docs_check, tree)
            log(`${st.docs_check} — exit ${r.code}`)
            if (r.code !== 0) throw new Wait(`${st.docs_check} exited ${r.code}: ${firstLine(r.err || r.out)}`, "red")
        }
        git(["add", "-A"], tree)
        if (run([GIT, []], ["diff", "--cached", "--quiet"], tree).code === 0) {
            d.result = { status: "empty", at: now() }
            log(`documents of ${d.prs.map((n) => "#" + n).join(", ")}: nothing to commit`)
            return
        }
        // the privacy check of what this commit adds to the tickets root, before anything leaves the machine
        const ecArgs = ["--changed", "--root", path.join(tree, root), "--base", `refs/remotes/${remote}/${st.branch}`]
        const ec = run(program(process.env.LAND_EVIDENCE_CHECK, [process.execPath, [path.join(__dirname, "evidence-check")]]), ecArgs, tree)
        log(`evidence-check ${ecArgs.join(" ")} — exit ${ec.code}`)
        // its findings are masked (two characters and the length), so the log may keep them
        for (const l of `${ec.out}\n${ec.err}`.split("\n").filter((x) => x.trim())) log(`  ${l}`)
        if (ec.code === 1) {
            const m = /evidence-check: (\d+) findings?/.exec(ec.out)
            throw new Wait(`evidence-check found ${m ? m[1] : "some"} findings in the documents, nothing pushed: the masked list is in ${path.basename(logFile)}`, "red")
        }
        if (ec.code !== 0) throw new Wait(`evidence-check could not run (exit ${ec.code}): ${firstLine(ec.err || ec.out)}`)
        const list = d.prs.map((n) => "#" + n).join(", ")
        git(["commit", "-q", "-m", `docs: mark the tickets of ${list} done`], tree)
        git(["push", "-q", "-f", remote, `HEAD:refs/heads/${d.branch}`], tree)
        const found = ghJson(st, ["pr", "list", "--head", d.branch, "--state", "open", "--json", "number"], "gh pr list")
        if (Array.isArray(found) && found.length) d.pr = found[0].number
        else {
            const body = `The tickets of ${list}, merged by land, are marked done.`
            const r = gh(st, ["pr", "create", "--base", st.branch, "--head", d.branch, "--title", `docs: mark the tickets of ${list} done`, "--body", body])
            const m = /\/pull\/(\d+)/.exec(r.out)
            if (r.code !== 0 || !m) throw new Wait(`gh pr create failed (exit ${r.code}): ${firstLine(r.err || r.out)}`)
            d.pr = Number(m[1])
        }
        log(`documents PR #${d.pr} on ${d.branch} for ${list}`)
    } finally {
        run([GIT, []], ["worktree", "remove", "--force", tree], st.repo)
        save(file, st)
    }
}
async function landDocs(file, st, madeThisRun) {
    docsEntry(file, st, madeThisRun)
    for (const d of st.docs) {
        if (d.result && (d.result.status === "merged" || d.result.status === "empty")) continue
        try {
            if (!d.pr) openDocsPr(file, st, d)
            if (d.result && d.result.status === "empty") continue
            let v = prView(st, d.pr)
            if (v.state === "CLOSED") {
                // closed without a merge: its tickets are not done on the main branch — a new branch and PR for them
                log(`documents PR #${d.pr} was closed without a merge, opening another for ${d.prs.map((n) => "#" + n).join(", ")}`)
                d.closed = [...(d.closed || []), d.pr]
                Object.assign(d, { branch: docsBranch(d.closed.length), pr: null, result: null })
                save(file, st)
                openDocsPr(file, st, d)
                if (d.result && d.result.status === "empty") continue
                v = prView(st, d.pr)
            }
            let sha
            if (v.state === "MERGED") sha = (v.mergeCommit && v.mergeCommit.oid) || "unknown"
            else {
                if (v.state !== "OPEN") throw new Wait(`the PR is ${v.state}`)
                ciGreen(st, v.headRefOid)
                sha = await mergeOne(st, d.pr, v.headRefOid, () => ciGreen(st, v.headRefOid))
            }
            d.result = { status: "merged", sha, at: now() }
        } catch (e) {
            if (!(e instanceof Wait)) throw e
            d.result = { status: "waits", reason: e.message, kind: e.kind, at: now() }
            log(`documents ${d.pr ? "#" + d.pr : d.branch} wait: ${e.message}`)
        }
        save(file, st)
    }
}

const waitingForCi = (st) => [...st.prs, ...st.docs].some((x) => x.result && x.result.status === "waits" && x.result.kind === "ci")

async function main() {
    const argv = process.argv.slice(2)
    const watch = argv.includes("--watch")
    const files = argv.filter((a) => a !== "--watch")
    if (files.length !== 1 || files[0].startsWith("-")) fail("usage: land <state.json> [--watch]")
    const file = path.resolve(files[0])
    const st = load(file)
    logFile = file.replace(/\.json$/, "") + ".log"
    const started = now()
    log(`land ${file}${watch ? " --watch" : ""}`)
    const deadline = Date.now() + T.watch * 1000
    const madeThisRun = { done: false }
    for (;;) {
        // a pass: the code PRs in order, then the documents PR once no code PR still waits for CI
        try {
            git(["fetch", "-q", st.remote || "origin", `+refs/heads/${st.branch}:refs/remotes/${st.remote || "origin"}/${st.branch}`], st.repo)
        } catch (e) {
            log(`fetch failed: ${e.message}`)
        }
        for (const pr of st.prs) await landPr(file, st, pr)
        const last = !watch || Date.now() + T.poll * 1000 > deadline
        if (!st.prs.some((p) => p.result.status === "waits" && p.result.kind === "ci") || last) await landDocs(file, st, madeThisRun)
        if (!watch || !waitingForCi(st) || last) break
        log(`waiting ${T.poll} s for CI`)
        await sleep(T.poll)
    }
    const lines = []
    for (const pr of st.prs) {
        lines.push(pr.result.status === "merged" ? `#${pr.number} merged ${pr.result.sha}` : `#${pr.number} waits: ${pr.result.reason}`)
        // no documents PR: the Evidence lines go into the tickets outside the repository by the orchestrator's hand
        if (st.tickets_root === null && pr.result.status === "merged" && Array.isArray(pr.evidence) && pr.evidence.length)
            lines.push(`evidence of #${pr.number} is the orchestrator's (tickets outside the repository)`)
    }
    for (const d of st.docs) {
        if (!d.result || d.result.status === "empty") continue
        const name = d.pr ? `#${d.pr}` : `documents ${d.branch}`
        lines.push(d.result.status === "merged" ? `${name} merged ${d.result.sha}` : `${name} waits: ${d.result.reason}`)
    }
    // while the main branch is red: one line with the culprit and the deadline of the fix forward
    if (mainRed) lines.push(mainRed)
    const all = [...st.prs.map((p) => p.result), ...st.docs.map((d) => d.result).filter((r) => r && r.status !== "empty")]
    const verdict = all.every((r) => r.status === "merged") ? "green" : all.some((r) => r.kind === "red") ? "red" : "unverified"
    st.runs.push({ started, ended: now(), land: verdict })
    save(file, st)
    for (const l of [...lines, `LAND=${verdict}`]) {
        log(l)
        process.stdout.write(l + "\n")
    }
    return { green: 0, red: 2, unverified: 3 }[verdict]
}

for (const [signal, number] of Object.entries(SIGNALS))
    process.on(signal, () => {
        log(`stopped by ${signal}`)
        unlock()
        process.exit(128 + number)
    })
main().then(
    (code) => process.exit(code),
    (e) => {
        unlock()
        process.stderr.write(`land: ${e instanceof Fail || e instanceof Wait ? e.message : e.stack}\n`)
        log(`error: ${e.message}`)
        process.exit(1)
    },
)
